# Build warnings

## Target

Full solution build produces **zero** compiler warnings.

## Current rule

| Rule | Required |
|------|----------|
| Build succeeds | Yes |
| **Warnings as errors** | Yes — `Directory.Build.props` sets `TreatWarningsAsErrors` |
| Fix warnings in files you touch | Always in the same PR |

## Agent

- Do not introduce compiler warnings (nullable, unused, obsolete, etc.).
- Do not claim "build is clean" without a verification result (`no-unapproved-runtime-execution.mdc`).
- At ship/PR: confirm a clean build via the selected verification provider or `direct-dotnet` fallback (`dotnet build BuildMonitor.slnx -warnaserror` when not claimed).

## User verification

```powershell
dotnet build BuildMonitor.slnx
```

Any `warning` that would previously have been non-fatal now fails the build.
